---
description: >-
  A top-level API group containing two nested subgroups (public, private)
  plus an ungrouped-icon gateway also placed inside the parent group, with
  services inside each subgroup connected across the subgroup boundary —
  exercising two-level group nesting with cross-subgroup edges.
---
architecture-beta
  group api[API]
  group public[Public API] in api
  group private[Private API] in api

  service serv1(server)[Server] in public

  service serv2(server)[Server] in private
  service db(database)[Database] in private

  service gateway(internet)[Gateway] in api

  serv1:B -- T:serv2
  serv2:L -- R:db
  serv1:L -- R:gateway
